You have designed the rate limiter using Token Bucket. Now suppose we deploy 10 instances of the Rate Limiter behind the API Gateway.
A user's requests can go to any of those 10 instances. How will you ensure the user's rate limit is enforced globally across all instances?


Rate-limit state cannot live only in the local memory of each RateLimiter instance. Otherwise, a user can bypass the limit by hitting different instances.

So we'd have:

                  API Gateway
                       |
          +------------+------------+
          |            |            |
          v            v            v
      RL Instance  RL Instance  RL Instance
          |            |            |
          +------------+------------+
                       |
                       v
                     Redis
                       |
                       v
                 Shared State

For Token Bucket, Redis would maintain the state for each rate-limit key:

user123:/api/search
    |
    +-- availableTokens
    +-- lastRefillTime
    +-- capacity
    +-- refillRate

Every RateLimiter instance operates on the same shared state.

