Two RateLimiter instances might receive requests for the same user at exactly the same time.
How do you make the refill + check token + consume token operation atomic in Redis?



We make redis operation lock


hen a request comes we make the allowed requeyss synchrnised so that we refull the bucket if needed..check tojem and ise token

Interviewer: That would work if all requests for a user hit the same RateLimiter instance, because synchronized only locks that JVM instance.

But in our distributed setup:

Request 1 → RateLimiter-1
Request 2 → RateLimiter-2

You could have:

Thread 1 → synchronized on Instance 1
Thread 2 → synchronized on Instance 2

Both can access Redis concurrently. So synchronized doesn't solve the distributed atomicity problem.

The correct approach is to make the entire operation atomic in Redis:

Refill tokens
    ↓
Check available token
    ↓
Consume token
    ↓
Update state

All as one atomic operation, typically using a Redis Lua script.



Redis Atomic Operation

1. Read bucket state
2. Calculate elapsed time
3. Refill tokens
4. If tokens >= 1
       consume 1 token
       return ALLOWED
   Else
       return REJECTED

Because Redis executes the Lua script atomically, two RateLimiter instances cannot interleave these operations.


